81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (In today's digital world, people use online platforms to communicate, share information, and find others with similar interests. However, many social platforms contain a large amount of information, making it difficult for users to discover communities that are actually relevant to them.The Community-Detection Platform is developed to solve this problem by providing a centralized platform where users can discover and participate in communities according to their interests. Users can create an account, enter their interests, search for communities, join groups, and interact with other members.The system can analyze information such as user interests, community topics, posts, and interactions to identify suitable communities. For example, a user interested in photography can be recommended photography communities, while a user interested in programming can discover programming-related groups.The platform also provides an administrator interface for managing users, communities, posts, and inappropriate content. This makes the system useful for educational institutions, organizations, hobby groups, and general online communities.The primary goal of this project is to create a simple and effective platform that improves community discovery and encourages meaningful interaction between users.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
