/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (COMMUNITY DETECTION IS AN IMPORTANT AREA OF SOCIAL-NETWORK ANALYSIS THAT FOCUSES ON IDENTIFYING GROUPS OF USERS WITH SIMILAR INTERESTS OR STRONG RELATIONSHIPS. SEVERAL ALGORITHMS HAVE BEEN DEVELOPED FOR DETECTING COMMUNITIES IN NETWORKS, INCLUDING LOUVAIN, LABEL PROPAGATION, INFOMAP, AND WALKTRAP. THE LOUVAIN METHOD IS WIDELY USED BECAUSE IT CAN EFFICIENTLY IDENTIFY COMMUNITIES IN LARGE NETWORKS. LABEL PROPAGATION IDENTIFIES COMMUNITIES BY ANALYZING THE LABELS OF CONNECTED USERS. EXISTING SOCIAL-MEDIA PLATFORMS ALSO USE USER INTERESTS AND INTERACTIONS TO RECOMMEND GROUPS AND CONTENT. THESE EXISTING TECHNIQUES PROVIDE A FOUNDATION FOR DEVELOPING AN EFFECTIVE COMMUNITY-DETECTION PLATFORM.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
